implementationPlan.description:
Opt-in absolute deadline MOE_PROXY_ONESHOT_DEADLINE_MS, plus its tests (src/index.ts, src/index.test.ts). This is the consumer contract WT-10 asked for in comment-8b75fe92: one bound over startup, connect, queued, sent and EOF drain together.
- Parsing, at startup before connect(): unset or blank means no bound, and every existing behavior stays. Otherwise the value must be plain decimal digits forming a safe integer (Unix epoch ms). Anything else fails closed: write one JSON-RPC error with a null id, `Invalid MOE_PROXY_ONESHOT_DEADLINE_MS: <reason>` (never echo more than 64 chars of the value), and exit 1 without connecting.
- When valid: one setTimeout at max(0, deadline - Date.now()) runs expireDeadline():
  - set shuttingDown, which stops reconnects;
  - clear the reconnect timer and the drain interval;
  - write exactly one error, 'Proxy deadline exceeded (MOE_PROXY_ONESHOT_DEADLINE_MS)', for each known pending id, sent or queued;
  - when no id is known yet (never connected, so stdin has not been read), write one null-id error with that message;
  - closeWebSocket() and exit 1.
  Ids are removed before writing, so no late success can follow.
- Step 1's drain caps every deadline at this one, so the earlier of the two wins with exactly one response per id. A signal still exits within 2s.
- Error handling: an expiry during the identity probe or a reconnect backoff exits the same way, and a deadline already in the past expires on the next tick.
- Tests:
  - never-connected: daemon.json removed, so the proxy is in its retry loop; deadline = now+1500 gives one null-id deadline error and exit 1 within 1.2-3s;
  - waiting: a blocking call the server answers at 4000ms, deadline = now+2500, gives one deadline error for id 1 at ~2.5s, never the late result, and exit 1;
  - invalid, it.each over 'abc', '-5' and '1e12' (each 'fails closed'): an immediate null-id error naming the variable, exit 1, and the mock server sees no connection.
